-- title:
--   Index scaling between two lattices in the twisted commutant
-- statement:
--   Let $K \subseteq L$ be number fields with $[L:K]=2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ is an integer power of $\sigma$, let $\delta_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ and $u$ a unit of $\mathbf{A}_K$, and put $\delta = \delta_0 \cdot c \cdot I$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K)$ (the image of $\delta_0$ under the left inclusion times the scalar matrix $c$). Assume the norm string $\delta \cdot (\sigma\delta)$, i.e. the product of $(\sigma_{\mathrm{GL}})^{i}\delta$ for $i < [L:K]$, equals the image of the scalar matrix $u I$ under the right inclusion $\mathbf{A}_K \to L \otimes_K \mathbf{A}_K$ ($hN$), and that $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x) \neq zI$ for all $x \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$, $z \in L^{\times}$ ($hns$). Fix a finite place $v$ of $K$, write $K_v$ for the completion and $\mathcal{O}_v$ for its valuation ring, let $\delta_v$ be the image of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, and let $T'_v = \{t : t\,\delta_v\,(\sigma t)^{-1} = \delta_v\}$, carrying a Haar measure $\tau$ for its Borel structure. Let $y \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be such that $y\,(1 \otimes g)\,y^{-1}$ lies in the twisted commutant $\{X : X\delta_0 = \delta_0\,X^{\sigma}\}$ for every $g \in M_2(K_v)$. Let $b : \iota \to M_2(L)$, $\iota$ finite, be $K$-linearly independent with $K$-span exactly $\{X \in M_2(L) : X\delta_0 = \delta_0\,X^{\sigma}\}$. Let $S_\Lambda$ be the additive subgroup of $M_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ generated by the matrices $(b\,i)$ with entries $l \mapsto l \otimes a$, $a \in \mathcal{O}_v$, and $S_M$ the additive subgroup generated by the $y\,(1 \otimes g)\,y^{-1}$ with $g$ an integral matrix. The conclusion is threefold: the relative indices $[S_M : S_\Lambda \cap S_M]$ and $[S_\Lambda : S_M \cap S_\Lambda]$ are both nonzero, and $$\Big(\int^{-}_{\{t \in T'_v \,:\, t = \sum_k (b\,k)\otimes a_k,\ a \in \mathcal{O}_v^{\iota}\}} \|N_{K_v}(\det t)\|\,d\tau\Big)\cdot [S_M : S_\Lambda \cap S_M] = \Big(\int^{-}_{\{t \in T'_v \,:\, t \in S_M\}} \|N_{K_v}(\det t)\|\,d\tau\Big)\cdot [S_\Lambda : S_M \cap S_\Lambda],$$ the integrands being the $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}^{\infty}$-valued norms of the $L \otimes_K K_v$ over $K_v$ algebra norm of the determinant.
--
--   This is the local commensurability step in the computation of the twisted orbital integral at a finite place $v$: the $\mathcal{O}_v$-lattice spanned by a $K$-basis of the twisted commutant of $\delta_0$ and the lattice $y\,M_2(\mathcal{O}_v)\,y^{-1}$ inside the same local algebra are commensurable, and the associated zeta-type integrals of $\|N(\det)\|$ differ exactly by the ratio of relative indices. It feeds the local covolume identity [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar).
